      "assessment": {
        "question": "### Exercise 4.12: Use equivalent fractions to solve problems\n\n3. The floor of a room is tiled with 64 identical tiles. A carpet is put in the centre of the room. The carpet covers $\\frac{3}{8}$ of the tiled surface. How many tiles are under the carpet?",
        "expected_answer": "$$\n\\frac{3}{8}=\\frac{\\square}{64}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times8}{8\\times8}=\\frac{24}{64}\n$$\n\nThere are 24 tiles under the carpet.",
